# Canvas UI and Asset Rules

For Phase 8B quiz UI, use Canvas/uGUI.

Do not use UI Toolkit for Quiz Portal, Available Quiz List, Quiz Instructions, Quiz Session Shell, item presenters, Submit Confirmation, Result Screen, Error/Retry, or Unsupported Item unless the project owner explicitly changes the requirement.

Use generated UI assets as sprites or sprite sheets.

Use sliced sprites for scalable panels and buttons.

Use Canvas, Canvas Scaler, Graphic Raycaster, EventSystem, RectTransform, Image, Button, Toggle/custom selection, ScrollRect, TextMeshPro, prefabs, and prefab variants.

Do not implement generated storyboard images as flat screenshots. Build structured UI from reusable sprite pieces.

Important text and quiz data must be dynamic TextMeshPro labels unless the asset is a deliberately static button with fixed text.

Use subject filters only in Available Quiz List: All, LiteraQuest, PE/Health, Science.

Do not build Term 1–3 as primary student filter chips. Term is row/detail metadata.

Modal/panel states should block background interaction and preserve list state when closed.
